{
  "name": "history-yy-end-with-offset",
  "description": "The eighteen-month transition of research/filers/siemens-india.md (2024-10-01 to 2026-03-31, after 1 October years and before 1 April years), numbered by 'start' with offset 1, so the years around the change are 2024, 2025 (the transition) and 2027. {yy_end} does not depend on the offset: it gives 'FY 2025-26' for the transition and 'FY 2024-24' for the year from 1 October 2023 to 30 September 2024. parse removes the offset before looking the year up: 'FY 2024-26' names the year 2024, whose last day is in 2024, so it is LABEL_NOT_RECOGNISED, and 'FY 2026-27' names the skipped number 2026. The first supported year (1 October 0001 to 30 September 0002) is numbered 2, so 'FY 0001-02' names a number below the supported range and is OUT_OF_RANGE. Illustrative.",
  "source": {
    "kind": "oracle",
    "citation": "Independent implementation of the spec in conformance/generators/fiscal_oracle.py, written with Python datetime and no fiscalclock code",
    "url": null,
    "checked_by": "fiscal_oracle.py: Calendar.seq built from the regimes and transitions; change_errors and naming_errors pass"
  },
